# ==============================================================================
# Cuebert LFS template for game projects — v1 (M5-P2)
#
# Engines covered: Unreal Engine 5, Unity, Godot (plus shared media extensions).
# Adjust commented stanzas for SmartMerge, Godot text scenes, or optional types.
#
# Drop this into your game project's .gitattributes.
# If you already have a .gitattributes, append this block below your existing
# rules.
#
# After installing:
#   1. Run `git lfs install` inside your project (once per clone).
#   2. Run `git add .gitattributes && git commit -m "chore: enable LFS for game assets"`.
#   3. Re-add any already-tracked files that match these patterns if you want
#      them to move to LFS going forward (they'll stay as regular blobs in
#      existing history; see `git lfs migrate import` for retroactive moves).
#
# Reference: https://github.com/ambtaylor/cuebert/blob/master/docs/_ai_system/standards/game-project-lfs.md
# ==============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unity SmartMerge (YAML merge) — optional
# If your team uses SmartMerge for scenes/prefabs, DO NOT LFS those types.
# Uncomment the next 3 lines to force text merge for .prefab / .unity / .asset,
# and REMOVE or comment out the three LFS lines for those extensions in the
# block below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# *.prefab merge=unityyamlmerge eol=lf
# *.unity  merge=unityyamlmerge eol=lf
# *.asset  merge=unityyamlmerge eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Godot — text-first option
# Many teams keep .tscn / .tres as normal text. If that is you, comment out
# those two LFS lines inside the machine block below (search for *.tscn).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Machine-installable block (do not edit markers — used by install-game-lfs.sh)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# <<<BEGIN_CUEBERT_GAME_LFS_V1>>>
# Unreal Engine binaries
*.uasset  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.umap    filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.ubulk   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.uexp    filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.pak     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Unity binaries (see SmartMerge notes above)
*.prefab  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.unity   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.asset   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.meta    filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.anim    filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mat     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Godot (see text-first notes above)
*.tscn  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.tres  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.res   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# *.import filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# ^ Judgment call: .import files are often small sidecars; uncomment if your
#   pipeline generates large imports or you want uniform binary handling.

# 3D models
*.fbx   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.obj   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.blend filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Textures / images
*.psd  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.tga  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.exr  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.png  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpg  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Audio / video
*.wav  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.ogg  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mp3  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mp4  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mov  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Archives (rare in-repo; listed for completeness)
*.zip  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Optional: lossless TIFF / BMP if your art pipeline commits them
# *.tif   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# *.tiff  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# *.bmp   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# <<<END_CUEBERT_GAME_LFS_V1>>>
